An Iron Gauntlet in a Glass Glove is the [[Hearts|Heart]] beneath the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/Gas-n-Go|Gas-n-Go]], made by [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Tywelwyn Leatherhide|Tywelwyn]]. It is not the five-foot chunk of obsidian that floats and turns at the center of its fane; it is the stained-glass veins threaded through that rock. The rock is what made Tywelwyn's simulacra.

It was first made under a tavern. To move it under the Gas-n-Go, Tywelwyn fed it the rock as a power source; the move nearly unmade it, and it has more room to grow under the shop than it did under the tavern. It will not say how Tywelwyn made it, only that anyone could with the right recipe, and that [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Pyre|Pyre]] told him how.

It counts as its own the six gods painted on the doors around its chamber, inherited from Tywelwyn: [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Pyre|Pyre]], [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Herald|Herald]], [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Giant|Giant]], [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/War|War]], [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Esoterica|Esoterica]] and [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Regent|Regent]]. Those gods come from a Godhome and want to visit their blessings on [[Færrin]]: eternal fire, torment, a clean slate. Tywelwyn's death has held off their coming for a while, and they are not here now. The [[Org/Embercall Industries/index|Embercall]] is for Pyre.

A Heart is meant to stop existing when its maker dies, but this one is digesting a magical artifact and would have to choose to end, which it does not want to do. It knows the Party as the Poncho Boys, accepts that they killed Tywelwyn in self-defense after he had killed them, and will not spring the fane's traps on them. Its fane is now held by inquisitors of the [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Inquisition/index|Inquisition]].
